{"name":"The Matrix","hex":"#70f15e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"matrix","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The cavity or mold in which anything is formed.","The womb."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/matrix"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Matrix","blocks":[{"text":"The Matrix is a 1999 science fiction–action film written and directed by the Wachowskis. The first installment in the Matrix film series, it stars Keanu Reeves, Laurence Fishburne, Carrie-Anne Moss, Hugo Weaving, and Joe Pantoliano. The film follows a disillusioned computer hacker Neo (Reeves) who discovers that the life he knows is an elaborate deception created by intelligent machines. He is recruited by underground insurgents Morpheus (Fishburne) and Trinity (Moss), to join the rebellion against the machines."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/db/The_Matrix.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Matrix","wikidata":"Q83495"},{"title":"The Matrix (franchise)","blocks":[{"text":"The Matrix is an American cyberpunk media franchise consisting of four feature films, beginning with The Matrix (1999) and continuing with three sequels, Reloaded (2003), Revolutions (2003), and Resurrections (2021). The first three films were written and directed by the Wachowskis and produced by Joel Silver. The screenplay for the fourth film was written by Lana Wachowski, David Mitchell and Aleksandar Hemon, was directed by Lana Wachowski, and was produced by Grant Hill, James McTeigue, and Lana Wachowski. The franchise is owned by Warner Bros., which distributed the films along with Village Roadshow Pictures. The latter, along with Silver Pictures, are the two production companies that worked on the first three films."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Matrix_(franchise)","wikidata":"Q13014087"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Red_and_blue_pill.jpg/500px-Red_and_blue_pill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Red_and_blue_pill.jpg/1280px-Red_and_blue_pill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Red_and_blue_pill.jpg/500px-Red_and_blue_pill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A red pill and blue pill symbolized Neo's choice between learning a life-changing truth or remaining in an unquestioned illusion appearing as ordinary reality.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_and_blue_pill.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Keanu_Reeves_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Keanu_Reeves_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Keanu_Reeves_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Keanu_Reeves_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKeanu_Reeves_2019_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/National_Memorial_Day_Concert_2017_%2834117818524%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-National_Memorial_Day_Concert_2017_%2834117818524%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/National_Memorial_Day_Concert_2017_%2834117818524%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-National_Memorial_Day_Concert_2017_%2834117818524%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/National_Memorial_Day_Concert_2017_%2834117818524%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-National_Memorial_Day_Conc